dy":"I'm not sure if my issue is related to this one, but it started happening after the same commit.\r\n\r\nWhen using [`coc.nvim`](https://github.com/neoclide/coc.nvim)'s functions `CocAction` and `CocActionAsync` with the following commands, I get a segmentation fault:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[1]    1746810 segmentation fault (core dumped)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe commands are:\r\n```\r\n\":call CocActionAsync('jumpDeclaration', 'drop')<CR>\"\r\n\":call CocActionAsync('jumpTypeDefinition', 'drop')<CR>\"\r\n\":call CocActionAsync('jumpImplementation', 'drop')<CR>\"\r\n\":call CocActionAsync('jumpUsed', 'drop')<CR>\"\r\n\":call CocActionAsync('jumpReferences', 'drop')<CR>\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt may have something to do with the with the quickfix, because each of these commands will fill the quickfix window. However, when using something like this, I do not get a segmentation fault:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\":call CocActionAsync('diagnosticRefresh', 'drop')<CR>\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm still trying to debug the command to try and figure out more about this issue.\r\n\r\nEdit: Just using the command `copen` will cause a segmentation fault. I'm not sure why the `diagnosticRefresh` command doesn't cause this.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/1219934315/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"lmburns","id":44355502,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzU1NTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44355502?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lmburns","html_url":"https://github.com/lmburns","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lmburns/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lmburns/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lmburns/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lmburns/starred{/owner}{/repo}","su